---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="FIFGO, Glen Hutajulu"
  description="A customer app and public website revamp for one of Indonesia's consumer finance groups."
>
<article>
<section class="cs-hero" aria-label="FIFGO and FIFGROUP">
<p class="cs-kick mono"><span class="sq" style="color: var(--acc)"></span>Case study &#123;02&#125; · FIFGO app &amp; FIFGROUP website · Consumer finance, 2023–2024</p>
<h1 class="cs-name px-font intro" aria-label="FIFGO and FIFGROUP"><span aria-hidden="true"><span class="c" style="--i: 0">f</span><span class="c" style="--i: 1">i</span><span class="c" style="--i: 2">f</span><span class="c" style="--i: 3">g</span><span class="c" style="--i: 4">o</span></span></h1>
<div class="cs-sub">
<p class="lede">A customer app and public website revamp for one of Indonesia's consumer finance groups.</p>
<a class="pill mono" href="#story">Read the story ↓</a>
</div>
</section>

<div class="cs-cover"><div class="cs-cover-in"><img src="/work/fifgo/cover.webp" width="2400" height="1600" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" alt="FIFGO app on a phone beside the FIFGROUP website on a laptop"></div></div>
<section class="cs-sum" id="story" aria-label="Project summary">
<dl>
<div class="rv"><dt class="mono">Problem</dt><dd>The website and customer app could not generate quality leads. Product information was inadequate, and the application and monitoring journey was too long and complex.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.08s"><dt class="mono">Role and team</dt><dd>UI/UX Designer at Aleph, working in a project team.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.16s"><dt class="mono">Outcome</dt><dd>In UAT, users completed the loan flow in under 7 minutes with zero drop-off.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><dt class="mono">Timeline</dt><dd>Sep 2023 – Feb 2024. The app and website are both live.</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Overview">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;00&#125;</b>Overview</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<p class="rv">In mid-2023 FIFGROUP decided to revamp its website and consumer app, to keep up with technology, hold on to existing customers and win younger ones.</p>
<p class="rv">Our answer was a set of tools that understand what people need, guide them through it and give them the confidence to go ahead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Research">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;01&#125;</b>Research</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">starting with the people</h2>
<p class="rv">We worked human-centred, in cycles of analyze, create and test, and started by listening to the business and its customers.</p>
<div class="stats rv"><div><b>38</b><span class="mono">Stakeholder interviews</span></div><div><b>3</b><span class="mono">Days of workshop</span></div><div><b>7</b><span class="mono">Journeys audited</span></div><div><b>4</b><span class="mono">Personas created</span></div><div><b>12</b><span class="mono">User test participants</span></div><div><b>2</b><span class="mono">Cities for user testing</span></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="band" aria-label="Personas">
<div class="band-head mono"><span><span class="sq" style="color: var(--acc)"></span>&#123;02&#125; Personas</span><span>4 personas</span></div>
<h2 class="px-font rv">four people, one worry</h2>
<p class="rv" style="margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.55; color: #B9BDC2">Taking on a loan is a big decision. Each persona was stuck in a different place, but all of them needed clearer information before they could commit. Across the research, security, relevancy and accountability mattered most.</p>
<div class="cards">
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.00s"><h3 class="px-font">young striver</h3><p class="who mono">Yoga, 24</p><p>Struggles to decide among too many unreliable loan options and fears unnecessary expenses.</p><p class="need">Needs step-by-step guidance and a clear amount and duration to pay.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.08s"><h3 class="px-font">family treasurer</h3><p class="who mono">Fatima, 37</p><p>Overwhelmed by detail and a long approval process, and can't find the product that fits.</p><p class="need">Needs digestible information and the ability to pick up where she left off.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.16s"><h3 class="px-font">assistance seeker</h3><p class="who mono">Ahmad, 44</p><p>Finds apps and manual form filling a hassle, and feels lost completing a journey online.</p><p class="need">Needs to be recognised as an existing customer and given relevant recommendations.</p></div>
<div class="card rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><h3 class="px-font">opportunity chaser</h3><p class="who mono">Okta, 34</p><p>Very busy, wants to anticipate the risk of failure, and needs assurance before committing.</p><p class="need">Needs flexible appointments and a tangible amount and loan duration.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Journey">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;03&#125;</b>Journey</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">three moments that mattered</h2>
<p class="rv">We mapped the main customer journey into three phases and set what each one had to become.</p>
<div class="phases"><div class="rv" style="--d: 0.0s"><p class="mono">01 · Discovery</p><h3>Be the effective discovery channel.</h3><p>Promo offers felt aggressive and disturbing. Customers wanted relevant, trusted offers at the right moment.</p></div><div class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><p class="mono">02 · Application</p><h3>Boost efficiency so sales can focus on converting bookings.</h3><p>Online applications were dominated by unintentional leads. Potential customers needed a simple, reliable process that encouraged them to apply.</p></div><div class="rv" style="--d: 0.2s"><p class="mono">03 · Monitoring</p><h3>Build a good relationship with good-performing customers.</h3><p>Reach to good-performing customers was low. They needed a trusted channel that gave them assurance about their finances.</p></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="hmw" aria-label="How might we">
<p class="mono">How might we</p>
<blockquote class="px-font rv">How might we provide a proactive, practical and clear platform for our users?</blockquote>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Application">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;04&#125;</b>Application</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">shorter steps to a loan</h2>
<p class="rv">To reduce the struggle in applying, the journey now runs straight from simulation into application, personal data is prefilled through OCR, and the form focuses on essential information.</p>
<p class="rv">The loan simulation works from either direction. People can start from the motorcycle they want, or from what they can afford each month, so they see a realistic amount and duration before committing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<figure class="fig rv" style="max-width: 964px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto">
<img src="/work/fifgo/loan-simulation.webp" width="1540" height="1214" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Loan simulation screens, by dream motorcycle and by monthly ability to pay">
<figcaption class="mono">Simulate by dream motorcycle or by ability to pay</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Contract">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;05&#125;</b>Contract</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">a contract you can actually read</h2>
<p class="rv">I revamped the mobile app's full loan-contract experience: application, payment, contract renewal, late fees and contract management. The old contract page was one long list of equally weighted labels and numbers, so we restructured the information around what customers look for first.</p>
</div>
</section>
<figure class="fig rv" style="max-width: 964px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto">
<img src="/work/fifgo/contract-before-after.webp" width="1600" height="1500" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Contract detail page before and after the redesign">
</figure>
<div class="ann">
<div class="ann-ph rv"><img src="/work/fifgo/contract-full.webp" width="517" height="2316" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Full redesigned contract detail page"><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 0.35%; width: 95.36%; height: 9.93%"><i>01</i></span><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 5.03%; top: 11.74%; width: 90.14%; height: 8.29%"><i>02</i></span><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 5.03%; top: 20.38%; width: 90.14%; height: 8.98%"><i>03</i></span><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 30.22%; width: 96.91%; height: 43.35%"><i>04</i></span><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 1.55%; top: 74.53%; width: 96.91%; height: 19.69%"><i>05</i></span><span class="ann-box" aria-hidden="true" style="left: 6.19%; top: 95.16%; width: 87.81%; height: 3.54%"><i>06</i></span></div>
<dl class="ann-list">
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.00s"><span class="mono">01</span><dt class="px-font">sticky header</dt><dd>A simplified, easy-to-find contract name and number.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.06s"><span class="mono">02</span><dt class="px-font">highlighted remaining bill</dt><dd>The most important information about the bill comes first.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.12s"><span class="mono">03</span><dt class="px-font">cross-selling card</dt><dd>Customers about to finish a contract see other loan products at the right moment.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.18s"><span class="mono">04</span><dt class="px-font">clear contract structure</dt><dd>Contract information reads easily with better categorised sections.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><span class="mono">05</span><dt class="px-font">quick actions</dt><dd>A dedicated section with visual icons, so the available actions are clear.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.30s"><span class="mono">06</span><dt class="px-font">floating payment button</dt><dd>Nobody has to scroll to the bottom of the page to pay.</dd></div>
</dl>
</div>
<div class="trio">
<figure class="rv"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/fifgo/app-home.webp" width="780" height="1688" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="FIFGO home screen with a motorcycle loan contract card"></div><figcaption class="mono">Home, contracts first · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/fifgo/app-contract.webp" width="628" height="2576" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="FIFGO contract detail screen with contract, cost and vehicle sections"></div><figcaption class="mono">Contract detail · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.2s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/fifgo/app-explore.webp" width="780" height="5477" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="FIFGO explore screen with product shortcuts, recommendations and daily check-in"></div><figcaption class="mono">Explore, products and rewards · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Website">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;06&#125;</b>Website</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">a website with more to say</h2>
<p class="rv">On the corporate side, stakeholders wanted FIFGROUP's online presence and content to feel more engaging. Inadequate product information was also part of the original problem, so the product page now leads with what someone wants to buy, then explains why to choose FIFASTRA, the four application steps and what to prepare. The group homepage starts from what the visitor needs and routes them to the right financing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<div class="pair">
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/fifgo/web-fifgroup.webp" width="1600" height="4902" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="FIFGROUP homepage with financing categories and need-based recommendations"></div><figcaption class="mono">FIFGROUP homepage · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure><figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/fifgo/web-fifastra.webp" width="1600" height="4120" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="FIFASTRA product page with motorcycle search, benefits, application steps and offers"></div><figcaption class="mono">FIFASTRA product page · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>

</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Visual language">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;07&#125;</b>Visual language</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">one visual language</h2>
<p class="rv">An icon set carries both function and character, and the same components keep the design consistent across every digital platform.</p>
</div>
</section>
<div class="pair">
<figure class="rv"><div class="panel"><img src="/work/fifgo/icons.webp" width="980" height="840" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Custom icon set for FIFGROUP"></div></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><div class="panel"><img src="/work/fifgo/components.webp" width="1600" height="889" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Reusable app components such as contract cards and payment summaries"></div></figure>
</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Result">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;08&#125;</b>Result</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">result</h2>
<p class="rv">In UAT, users completed the loan flow in under 7 minutes with zero drop-off. The FIFGO app and the FIFGROUP website have both been released.</p>
</div>
</section>
